# Upload context for `gcloud builds submit`. Docker has .dockerignore; Cloud
# Build reads this one, and without it the several-GB data/ directory would be
# uploaded on every build.
#
# gcloud does NOT fall back to .dockerignore, so the two files have to agree.
# They exclude the same things for the same reasons.
.env
*.local.*

.git
.gitignore
.venv
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.DS_Store

data/
docs/
# `etl/*` excludes the contents rather than the directory itself, which is what
# makes the negation below work. Excluding `etl/` outright cannot be undone:
# gitignore semantics -- which gcloud follows and Docker does not -- refuse to
# re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded. The two files agreed in
# wording and disagreed in behaviour, and Cloud Build found it at step 13.
etl/*
# ...except the vocabulary: app/contracts.py and app/prompts.py import it as
# the single source of truth for every controlled term, and the Dockerfile
# copies it.
!etl/vocab.py
scripts/
tests/
suggestion/
*.md
